WEBVTT

00:00.160 --> 00:00.680
City.

00:00.720 --> 00:06.800
Common table expression is a temporary named result set, like a virtual table, that could be used

00:06.800 --> 00:12.320
multiple times within your query to simplify and organize complex query.

00:12.360 --> 00:15.640
So let's understand what this means using the following sketch.

00:15.680 --> 00:19.560
So we have our database tables like orders customers and so on.

00:19.560 --> 00:26.080
And in very simple scenario we write a simple SQL in order to query and retrieve the data from the database.

00:26.080 --> 00:28.960
And then in the output we will get the results of the query.

00:28.960 --> 00:31.920
So this is the simplest version of querying data.

00:31.960 --> 00:34.080
Now things get complicated in our project.

00:34.080 --> 00:37.120
And we could have the following technique in our query.

00:37.120 --> 00:40.280
So we still have this section where we are saying select from.

00:40.280 --> 00:47.200
But now inside our query we can write another query like for example select from where, which is completely

00:47.200 --> 00:49.000
nothing to do with the first query.

00:49.000 --> 00:52.960
And we can give this new query inside our query a name CTE.

00:53.280 --> 00:58.000
And we can call this query a CTE query, common table expression.

00:58.000 --> 01:02.650
And the first query outside this city we call it a main query.

01:02.690 --> 01:06.370
Now if you check this, we have like a query inside another query.

01:06.370 --> 01:08.530
So now let's see what SQL is going to do with this.

01:08.530 --> 01:11.970
The first thing is SQL going to go and execute the city query.

01:11.970 --> 01:14.370
So the city query is going to be executed.

01:14.370 --> 01:18.170
And we're going to go and retrieve few informations from our database tables.

01:18.210 --> 01:21.610
Now the output can be available only in the query.

01:21.610 --> 01:25.850
And the output is going to have the shape of like a table like for example the sales.

01:25.850 --> 01:28.210
So now the sales table and the orders tables.

01:28.210 --> 01:35.650
Both of them are tables but one is stored in the database and the other one is an intermediate virtual

01:35.690 --> 01:36.250
table.

01:36.250 --> 01:38.610
So now what's going to happen in the main query.

01:38.610 --> 01:41.650
We can go and start querying the sales table.

01:41.690 --> 01:47.250
The result from the CTE as any other normal table like we do to the database tables.

01:47.250 --> 01:52.570
So the main query is going to go and retrieve few informations and maybe do some manipulations on top

01:52.570 --> 01:55.810
of the sales table or let's say the CTE results.

01:55.810 --> 02:00.850
And of course the main query as well can go and say you know what, let's go and query as well few tables

02:00.850 --> 02:02.020
from the database.

02:02.020 --> 02:04.540
So the main query has two sources of tables.

02:04.700 --> 02:11.140
Either get it directly from the database or get it from the table that is created inside the query.

02:11.140 --> 02:16.420
And then once everything is done, the final results of the main query are going to be presented for

02:16.420 --> 02:18.540
the user as a final result.

02:18.580 --> 02:25.220
So as you can see, the CTE query has one task where it generates like a table that lives inside our

02:25.220 --> 02:27.580
query, and we can go and use it as we want.

02:27.620 --> 02:31.900
So now this intermediate table that is created from the CTE has two features.

02:31.900 --> 02:34.220
First, this table will not live long.

02:34.380 --> 02:39.620
So once the query ends what's going to happen is going to go and destroy this table.

02:39.620 --> 02:41.500
So it will not be available afterward.

02:41.500 --> 02:43.660
And we are not able to query it anymore.

02:43.780 --> 02:46.020
So it's good he's doing here like a cleanup.

02:46.020 --> 02:50.260
And the second character about this, let's imagine that we have another side query.

02:50.260 --> 02:53.660
And it's retrieving tables directly from the database tables.

02:53.700 --> 03:00.260
Now if you say let's go and join those tables as well with the sales from the first query, well it

03:00.260 --> 03:04.990
will not be working because it's going to say, I don't know what you are talking about, and that's

03:04.990 --> 03:12.350
because the sales is only locally available for the main query in the same query.

03:12.470 --> 03:17.670
So that means it's not globally available like the database tables for any query.

03:17.710 --> 03:21.990
It is dedicated only for the main query within the same query.

03:22.030 --> 03:24.270
And now you might tell me Barra, wait wait wait.

03:24.270 --> 03:26.270
I have heard this story before, right?

03:26.310 --> 03:30.710
So this is an identical story to the one that you have told us about the subqueries.

03:30.790 --> 03:34.430
So what is exactly the difference between the subquery and the CTE?

03:34.550 --> 03:35.950
Well, you are totally right.

03:35.950 --> 03:38.950
The story is identical between the subqueries and the CTE.

03:39.230 --> 03:41.470
But still there are differences between them.

03:41.550 --> 03:43.190
So let me show you a few differences.

03:43.230 --> 03:44.750
Now let's put them side by side.

03:44.750 --> 03:46.510
We have on the left side the subqueries.

03:46.510 --> 03:48.550
On the right side we have the CTE.

03:48.590 --> 03:53.870
So now if you look on how we wrote the CTE and the subqueries, you can see that on the subquery we

03:53.910 --> 03:56.030
are writing it from bottom to top.

03:56.030 --> 03:58.910
So first we have this inner query the subquery.

03:59.270 --> 04:01.910
And then on top of it we have the main query.

04:01.910 --> 04:05.870
But now, on the other hand, the CTE, we are writing it from top to bottom.

04:05.870 --> 04:09.150
So first we write this inner query, the CTE query.

04:09.150 --> 04:12.630
And then beneath it we're going to go and write the main query.

04:12.630 --> 04:16.830
So this is the first difference between them on the way we write the query.

04:16.830 --> 04:20.110
So if I'm thinking about subqueries I start from bottom to top.

04:20.110 --> 04:23.190
If I'm thinking about CTE I think from top to bottom.

04:23.190 --> 04:24.430
But still you say you're not.

04:24.430 --> 04:25.870
I don't care how we write it.

04:25.910 --> 04:27.350
They are doing the same thing.

04:27.430 --> 04:33.790
The subquery is introducing an intermediate result that is used later from the main query.

04:33.790 --> 04:39.190
And the same thing for the CTE it presents like intermediate table that is used as well from the main

04:39.190 --> 04:39.790
query.

04:39.830 --> 04:45.790
Now let me tell you the big differences between them is that in the subquery the result can be used

04:45.790 --> 04:46.950
only once.

04:46.950 --> 04:52.950
So you cannot have another place in your main query where you go and reuse the results from the subquery.

04:52.950 --> 04:57.150
So you can use it maximum only in one position and only once.

04:57.150 --> 05:03.200
But in the other hand, with the CTE technique, you can think about the sales table as a virtual table,

05:03.240 --> 05:09.560
and not only you can use it in one place in the main query, you can go and use it in many other places

05:09.800 --> 05:11.680
so you can go and join it again.

05:11.680 --> 05:18.040
So that means I'm using the output from the CTE query in two different places in the main query, or

05:18.040 --> 05:19.760
maybe from three different places.

05:19.760 --> 05:25.240
So you can have another place where you go as well and query the sales table that is only available

05:25.240 --> 05:26.240
in our query.

05:26.240 --> 05:30.360
So this is the main and the most important difference between the subquery and the CTE.

05:30.400 --> 05:32.640
It's from the name common table expression.

05:32.640 --> 05:36.600
We think about the result of the CTE as a table.

05:36.600 --> 05:38.120
So we can go and select it.

05:38.120 --> 05:40.520
We can go and join it with any other table.

05:40.520 --> 05:44.560
So it is like a hidden virtual table lives inside our query.

05:44.560 --> 05:46.640
But the subqueries it's totally different.

05:46.640 --> 05:52.240
It's a result only for one position in the main query and it's used only once.

05:52.240 --> 05:57.920
So that means if you want the subquery in 2 or 3 different places, you have to go and write the subquery

05:58.120 --> 05:59.720
three different times.

05:59.720 --> 06:03.360
So now you understand why do we have CTE and why do we have subqueries.
